 "forward_eligible": false,
 "forward_eligibility_constraint": "Measures the drained per-descriptor ND2NZ service at the D128 and D64 GQA K/V geometries as a function of AIC concurrency and descriptor count under two source-address layouts. It licenses no interpolation across geometry, group count, descriptor count or layout. It is not Forward-eligible, and a counterfactual shows why: substituting these services into the FIA decode cold-drained branch -- even at an absurd 1 ms per descriptor -- leaves the predicted duration bit-identical, because that branch is computed and then discarded for decode shapes. The FIA decode prediction is dominated by its pipeline term (8.51 of 14.61 us at 8 blocks), and the MTE2 read term it would touch is 0.76 us. Consuming this data requires first changing which term prices FIA decode."
}
